# SABOTAGE: T42 - the RunWorker kill re-check (ADR-039 section 8.4, the
# "already-queued" half of the two-switch kill-switch double-check).
# DispatchWorker's own filter (status active AND disabled_by_operator_at IS
# NULL) refuses to ENQUEUE a run for a killed/paused workflow, but ADR-039
# section 8.4 requires a SECOND check at RunWorker start - "killed-while-queued
# work... finalize skipped/:killed, never silently dropped" - because a
# workflow can be killed AFTER a run for it is already queued (the race the
# dispatch-time filter alone cannot close). This patch neutralizes
# Samen.Automation.RunWorker.kill_switch/1 to always :ok, so an already-queued
# run of a killed workflow now FIRES instead of finalizing :skipped/:killed.
# The named red test - which enqueues a RunWorker job DIRECTLY for an
# operator-killed workflow (bypassing DispatchWorker, exactly the T39 F5
# methodology) and asserts the run finalizes :skipped/:killed - MUST fail.
#
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/automation/observability_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: an already-queued run of a killed workflow finalizes :skipped/:killed
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/automation/run_worker.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/automation/run_worker.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/automation/run_worker.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/automation/run_worker.ex
@@ -107,9 +107,9 @@ defmodule Samen.Automation.RunWorker do
     e -> {:error, e}
   end

-  # ADR-039 §8.4 double-check: active AND not operator-killed.
-  defp kill_switch(%{status: :active, disabled_by_operator_at: nil}), do: :ok
-  defp kill_switch(_wf), do: {:skip, :killed}
+  # SABOTAGE (T42): the already-queued-half re-check is bypassed - every run
+  # now proceeds regardless of the operator kill-switch (ADR-039 section 8.4).
+  defp kill_switch(_wf), do: :ok

   defp owner_actor(%{owner_id: nil}), do: {:skip, :owner_unavailable}

